From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci: wait after a denied cluster request in s2idle

In s2idle, when the firmware denies (PSCI DENIED) a CPU's request for the
cluster state, that CPU returns from cpuidle and asks again within
microseconds. On the Huawei MateBook E Go (SC8280XP), traces show the
other CPUs still inside CPU_SUSPEND at that point, counted as off by
genpd, so the returning CPU is the last one again and requests the
cluster again. Two to eight CPUs keep taking turns like this; about 99%
of the hops have no interrupt in between, and a ring can last until the
next wakeup, with the SoC out of its deepest state meanwhile.

Without a wait: 20 rings in a 10.8 h standby night with tracing on,
about 1,060 s in total, 13 of them lasting until a wakeup, up to about a
million re-entries in one sleep; 4 rings in a 4.1 h standby run with
tracing off, one of them about 381,000 re-entries, with 384,128 denials
(-EPERM) and 49 other failures (-EOPNOTSUPP) in s2idle. With a 3 ms wait
after every failed request: no ring in about 10.2 h over two runs, with
20 denials and 69 other failures. The second half of the 4.1 h run was
the 3.6 h with the wait on the same boot; only time of day differs, and
about 4 rings would have been expected at the first half's rate.

Busy-wait for 3 ms after a denied cluster request in s2idle, so that the
other CPUs are back before the next request. The other failures came at
about the same rate with and without the wait and are not part of the
rings, so they don't wait: the test kernels did, this change narrows it
to -EPERM. The normal idle path is not changed. Why the firmware denies
is not known, a shorter wait was not tried, and the wait applies to
every PSCI platform with OS-initiated cluster states: not for mainline
as it is.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index b250d0dde..193373e4a 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/cpuidle.h>
 #include <linux/cpumask.h>
 #include <linux/cpu_pm.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
@@ -61,6 +62,17 @@ static inline void psci_clear_domain_state(void)
 	__this_cpu_write(psci_domain_state.state, 0);
 }
 
+/*
+ * In s2idle, when the firmware denies (PSCI DENIED) a CPU's request for the
+ * cluster state, that CPU returns and asks again within microseconds. Traces
+ * on SC8280XP show the other CPUs still inside CPU_SUSPEND then, counted as off
+ * by genpd, so the CPU is the last one again and asks for the cluster again.
+ * Such a ring can last until the next wakeup. Wait a few milliseconds before
+ * asking again. Other failures, such as a return without powering down
+ * (-EOPNOTSUPP), don't wait.
+ */
+#define PSCI_S2IDLE_DENIED_DELAY_US	3000
+
 static __cpuidle int __psci_enter_domain_idle_state(struct cpuidle_device *dev,
 						    struct cpuidle_driver *drv, int idx,
 						    bool s2idle)
@@ -70,7 +82,7 @@ static __cpuidle int __psci_enter_domain_idle_state(struct cpuidle_device *dev,
 	struct device *pd_dev = data->dev;
 	struct psci_cpuidle_domain_state *ds;
 	u32 state = states[idx];
-	int ret;
+	int ret, rc;
 
 	ret = cpu_pm_enter();
 	if (ret)
@@ -87,7 +99,8 @@ static __cpuidle int __psci_enter_domain_idle_state(struct cpuidle_device *dev,
 		state = ds->state;
 
 	trace_psci_domain_idle_enter(dev->cpu, state, s2idle);
-	ret = psci_cpu_suspend_enter(state) ? -1 : idx;
+	rc = psci_cpu_suspend_enter(state);
+	ret = rc ? -1 : idx;
 	trace_psci_domain_idle_exit(dev->cpu, state, s2idle);
 
 	if (s2idle)
@@ -98,8 +111,11 @@ static __cpuidle int __psci_enter_domain_idle_state(struct cpuidle_device *dev,
 	cpu_pm_exit();
 
 	/* Correct domain-idlestate statistics if we failed to enter. */
-	if (ret == -1 && ds->state)
+	if (ret == -1 && ds->state) {
 		pm_genpd_inc_rejected(ds->pd, ds->state_idx);
+		if (s2idle && rc == -EPERM)
+			udelay(PSCI_S2IDLE_DENIED_DELAY_US);
+	}
 
 	/* Clear the domain state to start fresh when back from idle. */
 	psci_clear_domain_state();
